-- title:
--   A bottom-up computation with numeric tables on a rooted tree co-decomposition
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal T$ be a tree co-decomposition of $\sigma$-structures with bags $G_t$, adhesions $G_e$ and maps $g^e_t:G_t\to G_e$, rooted at $r$. Let $p$ be a list of numbers (a parameter, in the application the code of a sentence) and let $\mathrm{leaf}$ and $\mathrm{join}$ be functions from lists of numbers to numbers. The relation $\mathrm{CodeFold}(t,S,v)$ says that the number $v$ is the table held at the node $t$ once the set $S$ of nodes has been absorbed. It is generated by two rules.
--
--   1. **Base.** $\mathrm{CodeFold}\bigl(t,\{t\},\mathrm{leaf}(p,\langle G_t\rangle)\bigr)$, where $\langle G_t\rangle$ is the code of the bag.
--   2. **Step.** Let $e$ be an edge from $t$ to a child $c$ of $t$ with $c\notin S$. If $\mathrm{CodeFold}(t,S,v)$ and $\mathrm{CodeFold}(c,\mathrm{subtree}(c),v_c)$, then
--
--   $$
--   \mathrm{CodeFold}\Bigl(t,\;S\cup\mathrm{subtree}(c),\;\mathrm{join}\bigl(p,\langle G_t\rangle,\langle G_c\rangle,\langle G_e\rangle,\langle g^e_t\rangle,\langle g^e_c\rangle,v,v_c\bigr)\Bigr),
--   $$
--
--   where $\langle g^e_t\rangle$ and $\langle g^e_c\rangle$ are the lists of values of the two maps into the adhesion.
--
--   The arguments of $\mathrm{leaf}$ and $\mathrm{join}$ are passed as a single list in which each argument is preceded by its length (`frame`). The table of the root is any $v$ with $\mathrm{CodeFold}(r,V(T),v)$.
--
--   This is the bottom-up traversal of the proof of Theorem 1.16 with the tables and the operations on them left abstract. It separates two tasks: representing the tables of hypotheticals by numbers with computable operations, and running a bottom-up computation over a tree given as an edge list in time linear in the number of bags.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The relation has the shape of `CoDecomp.IsFold`, with numbers in place of hypotheticals. The codes of bags are those of `encBag`. The children of a node may be joined in any order.
-- source:
--   Bumpus, Gomes, Larios-Jones, Turner, Co-Decompositions and FO Model Checking, arXiv:2611.04658 (held file sha256 d550d7af…), proof of Theorem 1.16, p.41

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CoDecompFO_Lim
import Definitions.Def_CoDecompFO_Codes

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace CoDecompFO

open FirstOrder

variable {σ : Sig}

/-- Several lists as one: each list preceded by its length. -/
def frame (ls : List (List ℕ)) : List ℕ := ls.flatMap (fun l => l.length :: l)

/-- **A bottom-up computation with numeric tables** on the tree of a co-decomposition rooted at `r`
(Bumpus et al., *Co-Decompositions and FO Model Checking*, arXiv:2611.04658, held file sha256 d550d7af…,
proof of Theorem 1.16, p.41: "process the co-decomposition from the leaves towards the root, maintaining
at each node the reduced supported hypotheticals … Since each node is processed once, the total running
time is f_σ(w,|φ|)·b").

`T.CodeFold r p leaf join t S v` says that the number `v` is the table held at the node `t` after the
nodes of `S` have been absorbed, when a node alone gets the value of `leaf` on the parameter `p` and the
code of its bag (`base`), and absorbing the whole subtree of a child `c` along the edge `e` applies
`join` to the parameter, the codes of the bags of `t` and `c` and of the adhesion of `e`, the value lists
of the maps `g^e_t` and `g^e_c`, and the two tables (`step`). The arguments are passed as one list, each
preceded by its length (`frame`).

**Formalization Note** This is the shape of `CoDecomp.IsFold` with the hypotheticals replaced by numbers
and the operations by functions on codes, so that the tree traversal can be separated from the
operations. The children of a node may be joined in any order. -/
inductive CoDecomp.CodeFold (T : CoDecomp σ) (r : Fin T.b) (p : List ℕ) (leaf join : List ℕ → ℕ) :
    Fin T.b → Set (Fin T.b) → ℕ → Prop
  | base (t : Fin T.b) :
      CoDecomp.CodeFold T r p leaf join t {t} (leaf (frame [p, encBag (T.bag t)]))
  | step (t : Fin T.b) (S : Set (Fin T.b)) (e : Fin T.m) (he : T.IsChildEdge r t e) (v vc : ℕ) :
      CoDecomp.CodeFold T r p leaf join t S v → T.child e t ∉ S →
      CoDecomp.CodeFold T r p leaf join (T.child e t) (T.subtree r (T.child e t)) vc →
      CoDecomp.CodeFold T r p leaf join t (S ∪ T.subtree r (T.child e t))
        (join (frame [p, encBag (T.bag t), encBag (T.bag (T.child e t)), encBag (T.adh e),
          List.ofFn (fun x => (T.edgeMap e t he.top_mem x).val),
          List.ofFn (fun x => (T.edgeMap e (T.child e t) he.child_mem x).val), [v], [vc] ]))

end CoDecompFO


